WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:56.050
<b>Finale</b>

3
00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.350
[CHIEFTAIN]
What? They ran
away and left the island?

4
00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:57.790
[ISLANDER A]
Yes.

5
00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.050
We couldn't even give them our gift.

6
00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.510
[CHIEFTAIN]
How disappointing.

7
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.510
And after all they did for us.

8
00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:07.510
I wonder if they realize how
much we appreciate them.

9
00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.120
I agree.

10
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.990
They don't know how we feel.

11
00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.250
You know, Aisa, it's not fair
that you were the only one

12
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.170
that got to say goodbye to them.

13
00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.500
Everyone's really upset that we
let our heroes just run away.

14
00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.010
[AISA laughs]

15
00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.980
Luffy can stretch his body really far!

16
00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.900
He's like a "Gum-Gum Pistol!"
Kapow! Yay!

17
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.740
Aisa, please! You've got to hold still!

18
00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.280
I never knew there were warriors
like him in the Blue Sea!

19
00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.620
I wanna be just
like him when I grow up.

20
00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.000
A Gum-Gum warrior!

21
00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.070
[LAKI]
Aisa.

22
00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.720
[AISA]
Hm?

23
00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.630
I'm just going to
trim your hair a little.

24
00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.510
You need to let it grow.

25
00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.260
[AISA]
Huh?

26
00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.960
Hey, it'll look good.

27
00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.880
I think you've forgotten you're
a girl, and girls should look cute.

28
00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.760
What? Cute? Me?

29
00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.770
Are you nuts?

30
00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.980
[LAKI laughs]
I'm not!

31
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.670
With the war over, there's no need for
kids like you to carry weapons anymore.

32
00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:21.090
Now you can enjoy life the way it was
meant to be and as a proper young lady.

33
00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.510
I never knew you were so ladylike!

34
00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.930
[laughs]

35
00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.100
[LAKI]
Come on, Aisa! Now hold still!

36
00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.310
[AISA]
Laki's ladylike!

37
00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.220
[LAKI]
Aisa!

38
00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.480
[AISA, LAKI laugh]

39
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.990
[WYPER]
Great Warrior Kalgara.

40
00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:43.490
We were told that the Shandorians'
role has been fulfilled.

41
00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:48.930
As for your last wish it was
delivered to your best friend.

42
00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:52.730
Our future generations will
no longer have to shed blood.

43
00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.150
We are finally at peace.

44
00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.730
The war may be over.

45
00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:59.280
But one thing that will
never end is our pride!

46
00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.280
Please continue to guide us, Mighty
Kalgara, and watch over us as well.

47
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.370
We solemnly swear, The Fire
of Shandora will never die!

48
00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.930
I-I cannot abandon my duties!

49
00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.680
I am the Sky Knight, after all.

50
00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.610
Perhaps you should
be looking at yourself.

51
00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:29.740
Remember, this city originally
belonged to your people.

52
00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.700
[CHIEFTAIN]
It did, long ago.

53
00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.910
But that means nothing now.

54
00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.160
In fact, with this battle, all
of us realized something.

55
00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.040
Vearth belongs to no group.

56
00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.990
It must be shared.

57
00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:43.360
Our world has two sides.

58
00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.400
The land is called Skypiea.

59
00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.480
The city, Shandora.

60
00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:50.440
They have been torn
asunder by war for ages.

61
00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:55.780
Only a man who has long lamented that
war can unite them, and that man is you.

62
00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.490
So Sky Knight, Gan Fall.

63
00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:02.610
I'd like you to take
Skypiea's throne again.

64
00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.910
Only you can heal the deep wounds
that scar this land of ours.

65
00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.460
We'd like you to do it, too, sir!

66
00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.760
Gan Fall, please!

67
00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.300
We Shandorians are behind
you all the way Yeah!

68
00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.800
[SHANDORIAN C]
Gan Fall!

69
00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:16.800
[ISLANDER B]
Our god!

70
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.050
[ISLANDER C]
Please come back!

71
00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.020
[GAN FALL]
Well, well.

72
00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.090
And here I was thinking
that I'd finally be able

73
00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.640
to get some rest and
tend to my pumpkin patch.

74
00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:34.640
[CROWD cheering]

75
00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:50.910
<b>Lower Skypiea,
the White Sea</b>

76
00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.790
Okay! We're almost there!

77
00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.830
Everyone! See that up ahead?

78
00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.040
That's Cloud End!

79
00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.210
[USOPP]
Whoa, lemme see!

80
00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.420
[LUFFY]
Huh.

81
00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:07.300
So that's where we go back down from?

82
00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.220
[USOPP]
We got here sooner than I thought.

83
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.980
Aww. We really have to go back already?

84
00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:17.980
You know, it sounds crazy, but I'm
actually gonna miss this place.

85
00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.580
I think it's time we said
goodbye to the White Sea.

86
00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.750
[CHOPPER]
Sky island sure is fun.

87
00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.670
But scary, too.

88
00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.380
[USOPP]
We just go through that gate,
and there'll be a Milky Road that'll take us

89
00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.880
to the Blue Sea, huh?

90
00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:32.260
[NAMI]
Wonder if we'll ever
visit this place again.

91
00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.050
Well, you never know.

92
00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:37.010
[horn playing reveille]

93
00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.220
[PAGAYA]
I'm sorry, but this
is as far as we can go!

94
00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.470
Goodbye, my friends!

95
00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.510
Take care of yourselves!

96
00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:50.390
[SUU]
Suu!

97
00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:51.970
We will! Thanks for the escort!

98
00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.670
Conis! Don't forget me, angel!

99
00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:56.800
[USOPP]
Say goodbye to the others for us!

100
00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.900
See ya!

101
00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:00.970
It was nice meeting you guys!

102
00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:02.890
Thanks for everything!

103
00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.250
No! You've got it wrong!

104
00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:08.390
We're the ones who
should be thanking you!

105
00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.010
We'll never forget you!

106
00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:11.430
Thanks to you all!

107
00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.440
Goodbye, Conis, old guy, furball!

108
00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:14.940
Take care now!

109
00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:16.110
[PAGAYA, CONIS]
– Bye!
– Bye!

110
00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:17.960
Now take in your sails,
and hold on tight!

111
00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.880
You're in for a bumpy ride!

112
00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.420
Right! Let's do as the man says!

113
00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.420
It feels like we're
already picking up speed!

114
00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.220
[LUFFY]
Yeah, and we're sliding down from
thousands of feet in the air! Hurry up!

115
00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.220
[GROUP]
– Aye!
– Aye!

116
00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:31.090
– [SOUTHBIRD calls]
[GROUP]
– Huh?
– Huh?

117
00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:32.800
[SOUTHBIRD squawks]

118
00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.020
[LUFFY grunts]

119
00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.270
[USOPP]
Wh-What the...?

120
00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.330
[SOUTHBIRD squawks]

121
00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.670
He says, "Don't leave without me."

122
00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:41.920
[NAMI]
Oh.

123
00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.040
That's the Southbird we
brought up here with us.

124
00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:51.550
[NAMI]
Captain! It looks like the log pose has
the coordinates for the next island!

125
00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.640
Great! Let's go!

126
00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:58.930
Once we get to the bottom, we're
gonna start a brand-new adventure!

127
00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.030
Who's up for finding some gold?

128
00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:03.030
Guys! Get ready!

129
00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.340
Blue Sea, here we come!

130
00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.190
[GROUP]
– Aye!
– Aye!

131
00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.950
[GROUP yells]

132
00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.080
[GROUP laughing]

133
00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.290
Everyone grab hold of something!

134
00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.420
The freefall's about to start!

135
00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.450
[CONIS]
Heso!

136
00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:43.660
[GROUP screaming]

137
00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.080
Just hang on!

138
00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.080
One Octopus Balloon, on the way!

139
00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:51.920
[whistle blowing]

140
00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:01.340
[USOPP yells]

141
00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:04.400
[USOPP]
Octopus!

142
00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.310
What the...[grunts]

143
00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.360
[NAMI]
Oh! Oh, that hurt.

144
00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:13.970
What... happened?

145
00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:18.770
Hey, guys! Get a load of this!

146
00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:22.750
[ZORO]
What the hell is it?

147
00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.090
[CHOPPER]
A balloon!

148
00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:27.120
[LUFFY laughs]
Yeah! Ain't it great?

149
00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.500
[NAMI]
We're not falling!

150
00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.790
[USOPP]
Oh, good!

151
00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.040
For a minute there,
I thought we were goners!

152
00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.130
All of us!

153
00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.420
[bell ringing]

154
00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.090
[ringing continues]

155
00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:54.990
[LUFFY laughs]

156
00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:58.870
[ringing continues]

157
00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.480
[MCKINLEY]
Keep ringing it!

158
00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:07.360
Let the departing heroes of this land
know how much we appreciate them!

159
00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:08.610
[ISLANDER D]
Heso!

160
00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:09.780
[SKYPIEANS cheering]

161
00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:15.660
[ISLANDER A]
You're always welcome!

162
00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:17.160
[ISLANDER B]
Thank you so much!

163
00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:19.830
[SHANDORIAN D]
We wish you
safe passage to the Blue Sea!

164
00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.840
[CROWD chattering]

165
00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.250
[NARRATOR]
When you look up, you see the sky.

166
00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.880
Though some believe
it to be only a legend,

167
00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:37.850
there is an island floating
thousands of feet in the air.

168
00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:42.600
If you listen carefully,
you can hear the tolling of a bell.

169
00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:46.350
It rings today, and it
will ring again tomorrow.

170
00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:51.650
That bell rings from the heavens,
from a land that wandered.

171
00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:54.240
It sings of its pride, and proclaims

172
00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:59.160
to the rest of the world,
"We are here."

173
00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.700
[LUFFY laughs]

174
00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.250
This is so great!

175
00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:03.590
[USOPP]
Tell me about it!

176
00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.260
What a way to travel! I love it!

177
00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.980
[SHOJO]
You're calling off the search?

178
00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.070
[CRICKET]
Of course.

179
00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:15.110
The City of Gold has been
in the sky this whole time.

180
00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:17.820
There's nothing else to be
found at the bottom of the sea.

181
00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.190
Sorry, fellas. This dream's over.

182
00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:23.440
No point in staying here anymore.

183
00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.110
Old man.

184
00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.070
Cricket.

185
00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:31.310
[CRICKET]
I wanna thank all of you for helping me
pursue my dream for all of these years.

186
00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:33.390
You never stopped believing.

187
00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:34.240
That means a lot.

188
00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:35.460
[MASIRA]
Does this mean...

189
00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.410
[SHOJO]
...you're leaving the Alliance?

190
00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:39.650
[CRICKET]
Hey, guys.

191
00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:45.070
Since this dream's done, which
one are we gonna pursue next?

192
00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:47.530
[CROWD cheering]

193
00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:54.360
[MASIRA]
We'll all follow you to
the ends of the earth, Old Man!

194
00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:55.740
Yeah!

195
00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:57.370
[cheering continues]

196
00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:03.290
[GROUP]
– Gold! Gold! Gold! Gold!
– Gold! Gold! Gold! Gold!

197
00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.920
[LUFFY laughs]
We finally struck it rich!

198
00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.250
What should we buy with all this loot?

199
00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:11.460
Hey! I know! A huge bronze statue!

200
00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.760
Moron!

201
00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:14.750
Only an idiot would
exchange gold for bronze!

202
00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.880
How stupid!

203
00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.630
What we need are more cannons!

204
00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.130
Ten of them! Ten!

205
00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.020
[SANJI]
Nami, I want to buy
a refrigerator with a lock!

206
00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:23.310
[LUFFY]
Uh-uh!

207
00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:26.010
If you get one with a lock, there'll be
no way for me to get a midnight snack!

208
00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:28.390
[SANJI]
That's exactly why I want one, you pig!

209
00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.810
[NAMI]
Would you guys just hold on a second?

210
00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.350
We need to land first.

211
00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.450
Then we can divide up the treasure.

212
00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:36.820
Please buy me books!

213
00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:41.080
If we buy everything you guys want,
we're gonna be broke again in no time.

214
00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.020
[ROBIN]
Miss Navigator?

215
00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:44.060
The ship.

216
00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:46.050
Just where is it headed exactly?

217
00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.550
Where else? The next island, of course.

218
00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:52.770
[NAMI screams]

219
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.300
– You okay?
– What's wrong?

220
00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:57.070
Need a hug, Nami?

221
00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:01.580
[NAMI]
Dammit!

222
00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:05.420
We've been blown off course!
We must have hit an air current!

223
00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:06.420
[USOPP]
Huh?

224
00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.420
Well, I definitely feel a breeze.

225
00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:09.710
Is that a bad thing?

226
00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:11.210
Of course it is!

227
00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:14.510
Now we have no idea where we
are or where we're gonna land!

228
00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:18.720
And with the octopus up there,
we can't set the sails or control the ship.

229
00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:20.050
What are we gonna do?

230
00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:21.590
Hey, don't worry about it.

231
00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:25.140
Once we touch down, we'll just head
to the next island, easy as that!

232
00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:28.040
There you go, running
off at the mouth as always.

233
00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:30.010
[SANJI]
Hey.

234
00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:32.030
Sanji, what is it?

235
00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:34.790
Nah. Guess I was wrong.

236
00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.020
[USOPP]
Huh? About what?

237
00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:39.270
No. Never mind.

238
00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:41.190
[ZORO gasps]
We've got a problem!

239
00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:45.620
[ZORO yawns]

240
00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.220
Oh, yeah, it was just a dream.

241
00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.520
[NAMI]
Thanks for scaring us!

242
00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:51.560
[SANJI]
I'm gonna fillet you for that! I swear!

243
00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:55.020
[GROUP arguing]

244
00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.620
The sun's completely set now.

245
00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:07.200
It's still a nice view.

246
00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.510
[USOPP]
You're right. It really is.

247
00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:16.040
[PIRATE 207X]
What's all the ruckus out here?!

248
00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.910
Make way!

249
00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:20.950
Quit pushing! C'mon! Stop it! Lemme go!

250
00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:22.620
Why are they fighting?!

251
00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:36.020
Bellamy!

252
00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:37.400
Sarquiss!

253
00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:39.450
Isn't someone gonna stop them?!

254
00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:40.650
[SARQUISS pants heavily]

255
00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:43.510
No more! I'm begging you!

256
00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:45.410
Why are you making me do this?!

257
00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:46.810
What the hell is going on?

258
00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:49.620
I've never seen
Sarquiss plead like that.

259
00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.390
[DOFLAMINGO]
Why you ask?

260
00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:55.930
Why am I making you? Sarquiss. Bellamy.

261
00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:04.120
I'm making you do this because you've made
a mockery of this symbol. Heh heh heh...

262
00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.430
[DOFLAMINGO]
Does the Sky Island exist or not?

263
00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:11.270
Is the legendary
City of Gold real or not?

264
00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:16.540
The truth doesn't
really matter, now does it.

265
00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:21.060
You play the opposing sides off each
other, to twist them to your will.

266
00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:24.760
That's what I told you. Right, Bellamy?

267
00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:29.120
[PIRATE 207F]
I think that's, Don Quixote Doflamingo!

268
00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:31.790
[PIRATE 207G]
He's one of
the Seven Warlords of the Sea!

269
00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.410
I heard his bounty's over 300 million.

270
00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.460
What's a guy like him doing here?

271
00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:41.880
You've really let me down and I've got
zero tolerance for useless punks like you.

272
00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:45.500
No! Not again! My body's moving,

273
00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:50.810
on its own, I can't
control it! Please, nooooo!

274
00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:52.010
[slicing sound]

275
00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:55.720
– Bellamy!
– Bellamy!

276
00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:01.880
[BELLAMY]
Please.

277
00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:03.120
Huh?

278
00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:06.490
[BELLAMY]
Just give me one more
chance, to set things right.

279
00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:10.530
I swear we will loyally
follow your every command.

280
00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.640
Bellamy!

281
00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:13.540
Let it go, Bellamy!

282
00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.780
[breathing heavily]

283
00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:19.390
I might've lost but I have never
once acted against your principles.

284
00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:21.740
I swear on your symbol! Please!

285
00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:23.850
I had reasons for my actions!

286
00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:26.060
I couldn't just let the
Straw Hats get away.

287
00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:29.900
They were bound to find you
someday if I didn't stop them!

288
00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:32.540
Ahhh... What a touching sentiment.

289
00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:34.510
Such genuine loyalty.

290
00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:39.050
Your concern for my well-being
is duly noted, Bellamy.

291
00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:43.220
Heh heh heh... There's a
New Era quickly approaching,

292
00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:46.430
so your actions here
won't really matter.

293
00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:56.040
Doflamingooo!

294
00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.890
[slicing sound]

295
00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:02.000
[DOFLAMINGO chuckles]

296
00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:07.110
He wiped out Bellamy as easily as stomping
on a baby! He was worth 55 million!

297
00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.710
Hehehehe...

298
00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:10.880
The beginning is upon us!

299
00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:14.160
I suggest you prepare. We're
drawing close to a new world

300
00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:17.060
in which only true pirates can survive.

301
00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:21.640
The weak should run while they still can,
or be swept away by the tides of time

302
00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.880
as they roll back to reveal
a New Era of Champions!

303
00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:31.930
This is taking longer than I expected.

304
00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:33.300
[NAMI]
I agree.

305
00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:35.470
I'm really worried about
how far we've drifted.

306
00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.770
We could be anywhere.

307
00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:40.020
[SANJI]
What if I sang you girls a romantic
song to take your mind off th...?

308
00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:41.520
[NAMI]
Buzz off!

309
00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.520
[USOPP laughs]

310
00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:44.820
You know what?

311
00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:46.660
I betcha we get blown
all the way to Raftel!

312
00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:49.870
[ROBIN]
Uh, guys?

313
00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:51.870
Unfortunately, that's impossible.

314
00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:55.750
We'd have to sail across more than
half the Grand Line just to get there.

315
00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:59.520
[USOPP]
Uh... Yeah, um, I knew that.

316
00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.610
This conversation's boring.

317
00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.810
How much longer is this gonna take?

318
00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.520
Go to sleep.

319
00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.990
[LUFFY]
Hey, Zoro!

320
00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:11.840
If you're really bored, I've got
something you can do, and it's fun!

321
00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:13.470
Uh? Luffy?

322
00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:15.140
Where'd his voice come from?

323
00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:17.980
Good question.
He did sound kinda far off.

324
00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:20.110
Luffy! Where are you?

325
00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:23.360
[LUFFY]
I'm up here! C'mon, guys!

326
00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:26.580
This thing's a blast!
[laughing]

327
00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:29.200
What? Is he nuts?

328
00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:33.700
[LUFFY laughs]
Whee! Awesome!

329
00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:36.460
This is awesome!
[laughing]

330
00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:38.460
Hey, don't do anything stupid!

331
00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:40.420
All our lives depend on this balloon!

332
00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:42.050
You hear me, Luffy?

333
00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.840
[LUFFY]
Don't worry! Don't worry!

334
00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.150
[SANJI]
Luffy, stop! Get down!

335
00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.230
Right now!

336
00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.780
Sanji, what are you yelling about?

337
00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.280
[SANJI]
The octopus is shrinking!

338
00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.300
If we don't do anything, we'll fall!

339
00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:01.430
[NAMI]
Huh?

340
00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:03.300
[SANJI]
Hey, Luffy!

341
00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:04.300
What's that? Huh?

342
00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:06.170
[NAMI]
The octopus is shrinking!

343
00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.330
Shrinking?!

344
00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:11.880
You know, now that I look at it,
it does look smaller than it did before.

345
00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.210
[NAMI]
What are we gonna do?

346
00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.300
We're still really high up in the air!

347
00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:19.640
[SANJI]
Luffy! Something's wrong!

348
00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:21.260
You've gotta come down now!

349
00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.480
That was scary!

350
00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.950
Wonder why the octopus
isn't bouncy anymore.

351
00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:41.740
[SANJI]
I told you, it's shrinking, bonehead!

352
00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:46.580
[LUFFY]
Huh?

353
00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.080
[LUFFY]
Uh... That's weird.

354
00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.330
How'd the ship get below us?

355
00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:58.780
We're gonna hit the sea so hard,
we'll sink to the bottom!

356
00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.780
Only if the ship doesn't shatter first!

357
00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:02.570
Shatter? No way!

358
00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:04.740
Usopp, what are you gonna do?

359
00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.070
[USOPP]
What I always do!

360
00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:07.740
Save our lives, of course!

361
00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:11.870
[USOPP grunting]

362
00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:13.080
What are you doing?

363
00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:14.880
[SANJI]
Don't be crazy, Usopp!

364
00:20:16.670 --> 00:20:17.880
[USOPP]
Usopp...

365
00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.920
[yells]

366
00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:21.010
[GROUP]
– Huh?!
– Huh?!

367
00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.300
[USOPP yelling]

368
00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:26.470
[USOPP yelling]

369
00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:29.010
Hey! Look, it worked!

370
00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:30.060
All right.

371
00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.230
Come on, now.

372
00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:33.270
Breath dials! Do your thing!

373
00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:38.860
Now float! Float, I say!

374
00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:39.900
[yelps]

375
00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:47.350
We've slowed down.

376
00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:49.020
All right!

377
00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:50.520
Are we safe now?

378
00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.190
It sure seems like it.

379
00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:53.480
[USOPP laughs]

380
00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:55.900
Just leave it all up
to Usopp to save the day!

381
00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.530
[CHOPPER]
Usopp, you're so brave!

382
00:20:58.530 --> 00:20:59.740
[LUFFY laughs]

383
00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.950
I was actually scared
there for a second!

384
00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:03.030
[NAMI]
Me, too!

385
00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.790
Looks like we're finally safe!

386
00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:08.860
Or not!

387
00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:11.780
[GROUP yelling]

388
00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:12.990
[LUFFY]
Usopp!

389
00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:20.530
[LUFFY]
Everybody hold onto something!

390
00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:23.120
[GROUP yelling]

391
00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:32.250
[CHOPPER, USOPP grunting]

392
00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:34.920
[LUFFY]
Agh! That's cold!

393
00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:37.210
[SANJI]
Nami! Robin! Are you okay?

394
00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:39.740
[NAMI]
That was really scary!

395
00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:41.370
What happened to the octopus?

396
00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:43.120
[ROBIN]
Guess it ran out of air.

397
00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:44.870
[SANJI]
Wonder how that happened.

398
00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:49.630
[LUFFY]
Hey, come on!

399
00:21:49.630 --> 00:21:53.180
Don't whine.
We did make it down here alive!

400
00:21:53.180 --> 00:21:54.190
You're right.

401
00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:00.320
And we got to see an incredible place.

402
00:22:01.930 --> 00:22:04.970
[ROBIN]
Now that we're down
here, it looks so far away.

403
00:22:05.570 --> 00:22:07.410
[NAMI]
Like something out of a dream.

404
00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:09.200
It's a dreamland.

405
00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:10.910
Think we'll see it again?

406
00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:13.670
Well, you might see some
place similar when you die.

407
00:22:13.670 --> 00:22:14.790
Not you.

408
00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:16.850
I doubt you're going any place good!

409
00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:18.180
You jerk!

410
00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:20.520
[SANJI]
You guys keep discussing the afterlife.

411
00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:22.770
Me? I'm gonna go
put on a pot of coffee.

412
00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:24.480
[LUFFY]
Make dinner instead, Sanji!

413
00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.780
[SANJI]
Are you ever not hungry?

414
00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:28.490
Have some coffee first
and be patient, will ya!

415
00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:29.740
[LUFFY]
Okay.

416
00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:32.080
Hey, by the way...

417
00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:38.250
[sirens blaring]

418
00:22:50.030 --> 00:22:54.660
[LUFFY]
...does anybody know...
just where the heck we are?

419
00:22:58.210 --> 00:23:03.730
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

420
00:23:03.950 --> 00:23:09.150
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

421
00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:11.950
You are so much like the moon

422
00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:16.600
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

423
00:23:20.050 --> 00:23:29.000
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

424
00:23:29.060 --> 00:23:34.230
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

425
00:23:34.230 --> 00:23:42.540
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

426
00:23:43.180 --> 00:23:49.430
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

427
00:23:49.430 --> 00:23:55.050
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

428
00:23:56.290 --> 00:24:00.820
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

429
00:24:00.820 --> 00:24:07.210
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
